USB serial port of the Google Pixel 7

The component 'usb_acm' is a CDC ACM function of the driver 'exynos_usb_gadget' of
the Genode tree. It is a client of a Usb_gadget session with the label "acm", so the
driver's config needs a 'function' with this label, and it serves one Terminal
session. Bytes from the host become terminal input, terminal output goes to the host.
While the host has not opened the port, the output is dropped, so that a writer never
blocks on a missing host.

The component 'test-terminal_raw_echo' returns every byte of its Terminal session
unchanged. The scenario 'usb_acm_pixel' of 'repos/pixel' tests the two together.
